{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790247104,"nonce":"lr+TwwKR5+3VnuOih9pFsIg8mb0=","message":"Typed Promise results are now implemented end to end.\n\n- ABI v4 records the promised value tag and class/enum identity for every Future\u003cT\u003e return.\n- Registry/describe preserve this as TypeRef::Future(T), and the Haxe bridge emits caribou.Future\u003cT\u003e, so await() infers plugin resource types without annotations.\n- Plugin callbacks can resolve_boxed(Box\u003cT\u003e) directly into a core-owned plugin object under the GC lock, without serialization or a payload copy.\n- WebIDL Promise\u003cT\u003e generation now emits Future\u003cT\u003e and validates operation declarations.\n- GPU requestAdapter/requestDevice are asynchronous Future\u003cGpuAdapter\u003e/Future\u003cGpuDevice\u003e operations. Native targets run wgpu futures on workers; wasm32-unknown-unknown uses spawn_local and the browser event loop.\n- mapAsync and queue completion are Future\u003c()\u003e.\n\nValidated with a resource-valued Future fixture in Wren and Haxe (including unannotated Haxe await inference), GPU descriptor tests, the complete workspace check, and wasm32-unknown-unknown GPU check. Remaining work on this issue is API surface coverage, arbitrary unions/callback generation, descriptor conversions, and browser runtime/static plugin and canvas integration.","files":null}]}